\title{Empirical risk}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Let #{\mu} be a distribution, #{h \in \mathcal{F}}. Then the \em{empirical risk} with respect to some finite collection of samples #{\lbrace (x, y)\rbrace  = S} sampled from #{\mu} is defined by}

##{\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_S(h) = \frac{1}{|S|}\sum_{(x,y) \in S} \ell(h(x), y).}
